WEBVTT

00:05:59.708 --> 00:06:03.538
And so I'll walk into
a room with 4,000 people,

00:06:03.562 --> 00:06:06.227
and they look like the most boring
63-year-old white men

00:06:06.251 --> 00:06:08.131
you could ever imagine, in gray suits,

00:06:08.155 --> 00:06:11.795
and I'm about to talk to them about
the love life of George Eliot

00:06:11.819 --> 00:06:14.652
or something really emotional
and gooey and woo-woo.

00:06:14.676 --> 00:06:17.466
And I walk into that room
and I look over these bored faces

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:20.620
who've been talking about
health benefits for the last three days,

00:06:20.644 --> 00:06:21.892
and I think to myself,

00:06:21.916 --> 00:06:23.522
"This is not going to go well."

00:06:23.546 --> 00:06:25.309
And then I start talking about it.

00:06:25.333 --> 00:06:28.871
And then I start talking about
the hard moments in my own life,

00:06:28.895 --> 00:06:32.653
and there's a quality of silence
that occurs none of the other times